Actually, let me look at the `error:` path. When `p==end`, then `*p` dereferences `end` which is out of bounds. That's the "missing safety checks for log messages when the message buffer is not being parsed" - the `LM_ERR("parse error near char [%d][%c]\n", *p, *p)` dereferences `*p` even when `p==end`.

